### Subagent return contract (trust the result; match the signal, not the wording)

Trust the worker's reported result verbatim — a `PASS` means passed; do not re-verify. Match on the
**signal**, not the exact phrasing: the forms below are the **canonical** shape, but accept any equivalent
wording that carries the same signal. Do not force a re-emit over harmless phrasing.

| Subagent | Expected signal (canonical form) |
| --- | --- |
| **refactorer** | completion + file list — `Step N done. Files: [list].` (fix loops carry no step number: accept any completion line + file list, e.g. `Fix done. Files: …` or `Checklist step N done. …`) |
| **verifier** | `PASS` — or `FAIL` + bullet list |
| **tester** | `PASS` — or `FAIL` + minimal RCA |
| **test-writer** | tests-done + file list — `Finalize tests done. Files: [list].` (also accept `Finalize coverage pass tests done. …`) — or `UNTESTABLE: <reason>` |
| **doc-writer** | `Finalized docs: <branch doc> + CHANGELOG` (+ ` + README` if touched) — or per `.cursor/agents/doc-writer.md` |

Re-emit is a last resort: ask again **only** when the signal itself is missing (no `PASS`/`FAIL`, no
`done`/completion line, no `UNTESTABLE`) or is buried in prose — never for a wording variant. Do not paraphrase.

### Fix-loop spawn order (reuse after CI/Bugbot/coverage failures)

1. **refactorer** (fix template) → 2. **verifier** (production) → 3. **tester** (PHPUnit + PHPStan) → 4. **tester** (final E2E) → commit → push → re-watch CI (and re-trigger Bugbot if needed).

Coverage gap pass only: **test-writer** → **verifier** (test files only) → **tester** (PHPUnit + PHPStan).

## Sequence

> **Bugbot in the cloud:** the local `/review-bugbot` subagent is not available to API-launched cloud
> agents (`subagent_type: "bugbot"` fails there), so this phase uses the GitHub-App **PR Bugbot**,
> triggered explicitly with a `bugbot run` comment on the PR (step 4). Review rules: `.cursor/BUGBOT.md`.

1. **Push + PR** — `git push -u origin HEAD`; `gh pr create --base <base branch from your launch prompt>`
   with the `<!-- metadata -->` block (labels, milestone, `Closes #XXX`). This triggers the PR CI checks.
2. **CI quality gate** — wait on the PR's status checks for this branch yourself (a watch, not a test —
   no tester needed). `gh pr checks` covers every required gate (the PHP Tests jobs, `infection-diff`,
   `e2e-smoke`, `frontend`) rather than a single workflow:
   ```bash
   gh pr checks <pr> --watch --fail-fast
   ```
   FAIL → fix-loop spawn order (production path above), commit, push, re-watch until green.
3. **Coverage gap pass** (optional advisory; after CI green, before Bugbot) — Codecov posts a per-PR
   patch-coverage comment only after step 2 completes. Run this pass **only when all** apply:
   - Ticket `## TESTING STRATEGY` does **not** mark the ticket `test-writer: skip`, **and**
   - The latest `codecov` bot comment on the PR lists at least one **testable** uncovered production file
     under `app/` or `packages/` (not views, not version-only `app/system/config.php` bumps).
   When triggered:
   1. Poll for the latest Codecov comment (newest `author.login == "codecov"` on the PR):
      `gh pr view <pr> --comments --json comments --jq '[.comments[] | select(.author.login=="codecov")] | last'`
      If none appears within ~5 min after CI green, skip this step.
   2. Filter the comment's file list — drop `views/`, `app/system/config.php` (version-only), and any
      path the ticket defers. Build production scope from `git diff <base>...HEAD -- app/ packages/`.
   3. Spawn **test-writer** (coverage gap template).
   4. Spawn **verifier** (test files only template).
   5. Spawn **tester** (PHPUnit + PHPStan template).
   On FAIL at 4 or 5: **test-writer** (retry template), then re-run 4 → 5; if clearly a production regression
   → fix-loop spawn order (production path).
   On PASS: `git commit` (`test(<scope>): close codecov patch gaps`), push, re-watch step 2 to green.
   **At most one** coverage-gap iteration per Finalize run (Stuck-breaker still applies). If test-writer
   returns `UNTESTABLE` for all gaps, skip the commit and proceed to step 4.
4. **PR-Bugbot review** — CI is green, so trigger the review: `gh pr comment <pr> --body "bugbot run"`,
   then wait for the `Cursor Bugbot` status check (e.g. `gh pr checks <pr> --watch`). Read findings via
   `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/<pr>/comments` (or `gh pr view <pr> --comments`). Findings →
   fix-loop spawn order → commit → push; a fix re-runs CI, so re-watch step 2 to green, then re-comment
   `bugbot run` — repeat until Bugbot is clean **and** CI is green.
5. **Finalize** (follow `push.mdc`, but delegate the writing) — in this order:
   1. **Version bump** (you) — run the `version-bump` skill → `app/system/config.php` (once per PR).
   2. Spawn **doc-writer** (Finalize docs template).
   3. **PHASE Deferred sync (you)** — if the ticket / branch-doc `## Deferred` (or ticket Bridges) is
      non-empty, open each named future step in `migration-docs/TODO/PHASE_*_MODERNISING.md` and confirm
      the work item is present as **forward-only what + why** (no completed-step / ticket / PR narration).
      Missing → amend before the ROADMAP commit (same prose rules as Architect Responsibility 6). Unclear
      target step → `ESCALATE`. Skip when Deferred is empty / non-goal only. (Plan should have done this;
      this is the safety net.)
   4. **ROADMAP closure** (you) — update `.cursor/ROADMAP.md` (header pointer, this step's row
      Status/Audit/PR, Phase 1 audit closures per `push.mdc`).
   5. **Commit + archive** (you) — commit per `push.mdc` (`chore(release): bump version to X.Y.Z` for
      config + CHANGELOG + branch doc; `docs(roadmap): …` for the ROADMAP — include any PHASE amend from
      step 3 in the docs commit), then archive the ticket:
      `git mv migration-docs/tickets/active/{task-slug}_plan.md migration-docs/tickets/done/`, and
      `git push` (second push). Do not merge.

